-- IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md §11.19, defect OF-7: an @export whose read-set
-- crosses an IMPORT is refused.
--
-- `implicit-rate-lib` declares a section GIVEN `the rate` and a rule that reads
-- it. This module imports that rule and exports something that calls it.
-- Discharge does not cross an IMPORT, so all three of these are true at once
-- and none of them is visible to the writer:
--
--   * `the rate` appears in no schema this export publishes, so
--     `l4 batch --validate-only` answers {"errors":[],"status":"valid"} for a
--     row that provably cannot evaluate;
--   * a value sent under that name is accepted into the row and then dropped,
--     because nothing binds it; and
--   * `l4 batch` could not deliver it even if the schema demanded it: it
--     supplies a binder by rewriting this module's own source, and the IMPORT
--     is re-emitted verbatim, so the imported module is re-resolved from disk
--     untouched.
--
-- The refusal comes BEFORE closing the read-set collector over imports, which
-- is the ruled end state (R-X3). Closing it first would turn a false green into
-- a parameter demanded and then silently ignored, which is worse.
--
-- Calling an imported reader WITHOUT exporting it is fine and stays fine:
-- `ok/section-given-import-call.l4` pins that.

IMPORT `implicit-rate-lib`

@export What this amount comes to at the imported rate.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cost of` amount MEANS `scaled by the rate` amount
